  "function": {
    "uniprot_function": "Component of the Wnt-Fzd-LRP5-LRP6 complex that triggers beta-catenin signaling through inducing aggregation of receptor-ligand complexes into ribosome-sized signalsomes. The beta-catenin signaling pathway leads to the activation of disheveled proteins, inhibition of GSK-3 kinase, nuclear accumulation of beta-catenin and activation of Wnt target genes. Plays a role as a receptor or coreceptor for Wnt and thereby transmits the canonical Wnt/beta-catenin signaling cascade. Cell-surface coreceptor of Wnt/beta-catenin signaling, which plays a pivotal role in bone formation. Essential for proper development of different organs in vertebrates including cell proliferation, specification, migration, and embryonic development.",
    "catalytic_activity": "Not applicable (receptor/coreceptor, not an enzyme)",
    "subcellular_location": ["Plasma membrane", "Endoplasmic reticulum (during processing)", "Cell membrane"],
    "tissue_specificity": "Highly expressed in heart, pancreas, placenta, ovary, lung, brain, and kidney. Northern blot detected 10-kb transcript in variety of tissues. Shows cytoplasmic and membranous expression with granular pattern in all tissues.",
