    "pathway_role_summary": "LRP6 is the essential coreceptor for canonical Wnt signaling. It forms a ternary complex with Wnt ligands and Frizzled receptors to initiate signaling. Upon Wnt binding, LRP6 is phosphorylated by CK1 and GSK3beta, creating docking sites for Axin. This recruits the beta-catenin destruction complex to the membrane, preventing beta-catenin degradation and allowing nuclear accumulation to activate Wnt target genes. LRP6 is inhibited by secreted antagonists including Dickkopf (DKK1/2), sclerostin (SOST), and Wise. LRP6 plays critical roles in embryonic development, bone formation, and tissue homeostasis."
  },
