    "data_quality_notes": "High-quality data available from multiple sources. Extensive structural characterization with 7+ PDB entries covering extracellular domains. Comprehensive phosphorylation site mapping. Full protein sequence not included in JSON but available at UniProt. Some InterPro/Pfam domain boundaries are approximate. IntAct interaction accessions not directly accessible but interactions confirmed through literature. STRING network visualization not directly accessible via API but top interactors extracted from literature.",
    "modeling_relevance_summary": "LRP6 is a central node in canonical Wnt/beta-catenin signaling pathway. Critical for modeling: (1) Five reiterated PPPSPxS motifs in intracellular domain phosphorylated by CK1 and GSK3beta create switch-like behavior; (2) Phosphorylation-dependent recruitment of Axin/GSK3B complex to membrane is key regulatory step; (3) Multiple negative regulators (DKK1/2, SOST, Wise) provide multiple points of pathway control; (4) Transmembrane receptor with large extracellular domain for ligand binding and short intracellular domain for signaling; (5) Cooperates with Frizzled receptors in ternary complex formation with Wnt ligands; (6) Post-translational modifications (phosphorylation, ubiquitination, glycosylation, acetylation) provide multiple regulatory layers; (7) Essential for beta-catenin stabilization and nuclear translocation. Key for rule-based modeling of Wnt pathway dynamics including signalosome assembly, destruction complex recruitment, and beta-catenin regulation."
  }
